# EtAlertBanner Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtAlertBanner` is a full-width inline alert surface for communicating an account/state-level condition that needs the user's attention (e.g. account liquidation, restrictions). It renders an icon + title + description, with an optional trailing CTA link and/or a whole-banner press handler.

It is **not** the same as `EtBanner`:

- `EtBanner` (`components/feedback/banner/`) — promo/marketing compound banner (Title/Description/Actions/Illustration + dismiss), no severity concept, fixed `cardDefault` background.
- `EtAlertBanner` — severity-driven alert (colored fill per severity), simple props API, no compound children.

If your design calls for a dismissible promo card with an illustration, use `EtBanner`, not `EtAlertBanner`.

## Entry Point & Contract

```tsx
<EtAlertBanner
  severity: AlertBannerSeverity     // currently only 'warning'
  icon: string                      // EtIconV2 icon name
  title: string
  description: string
  ctaLabel?: string
  onCtaPress?: () => void
  onPress?: () => void
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
/>
```

| Prop                 | Type                    | Default | Notes                                                                              |
| -------------------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `severity`           | `AlertBannerSeverity`   | —       | Only `'warning'` exists today (PBD-944). Drives background/icon/text color tokens.  |
| `icon`               | `string`                | —       | Forwarded to `EtIconV2`'s `name` prop, rendered at size 20.                         |
| `title`              | `string`                | —       | Bold single-line-ish heading, `label-primary-semibold`.                            |
| `description`        | `string`                | —       | Supporting copy, `body-secondary-regular`.                                         |
| `ctaLabel`           | `string`                | —       | When set, renders a trailing pressable text CTA in `colors.primary600`.            |
| `onCtaPress`         | `() => void`            | —       | Handler for the CTA press. Ignored if `ctaLabel` is omitted.                        |
| `onPress`            | `() => void`            | —       | When set, wraps the whole banner in a `Pressable` (`{testID}-pressable`).           |
| `style`              | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>`  | —       | Merged onto the outer container, after the severity background color.              |
| `testID`             | `string`                | —       | Root testID; derives `{testID}-title`, `{testID}-description`, `{testID}-cta`, `{testID}-pressable`. |
| `accessibilityLabel` | `string`                | —       | Defaults to `` `${title}. ${description}` `` on the `accessibilityRole="alert"` container. |

## Usage Patterns

### Informational alert, no CTA

```tsx
import { EtAlertBanner } from 'etoro-ui';

<EtAlertBanner severity="warning" icon="info-circle" title="Account Liquidated" description="You can't perform any trading activity until you deposit." />;
```

### With a CTA that opens a sheet/screen

```tsx
<EtAlertBanner
  severity="warning"
  icon="info-circle"
  title={t('liquidation.banner.title')}
  description={t('liquidation.banner.description')}
  ctaLabel={t('liquidation.banner.learnMore')}
  onCtaPress={() => sheetStore.open(LiquidationSheetMode.LIQUIDATION)}
  testID="liquidation-banner-home"
/>
```

### Whole-banner press (no separate CTA)

```tsx
<EtAlertBanner severity="warning" icon="info-circle" title="Action needed" description="Tap to review." onPress={openDetails} />
```

## Anti-patterns

### Don't use this for promo/marketing content

```tsx
// BAD — no severity/urgency, just marketing copy
<EtAlertBanner severity="warning" icon="gift" title="20% off Club" description="Upgrade today" />
```

**Fix:** Use `EtBanner` for promotional/dismissible content instead.

### Don't pass both `onPress` and rely on the CTA for the same action

Wrapping the whole banner in `onPress` while also wiring `onCtaPress` to a different action can be confusing for screen reader users, since the container announces as `accessibilityRole="alert"` while nesting an interactive `Pressable` CTA. Prefer one primary interaction per banner.

## Design Tokens

Severity color resolution lives in `et-alert-banner.styles.ts` (`getAlertBannerSeverityStyles`). Today only `'warning'` is implemented:

| Element    | Token                        |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- |
| Background | `colors.accentF100`          |
| Icon       | `colors.accentG700`          |
| Text       | `colors.textPrimaryNeutral`  |
| CTA text   | `colors.primary600`          |

Spacing uses `X1`/`X3`/`X4` tokens from `core/styles`.

## Accessibility

- Root container has `accessibilityRole="alert"` so assistive tech announces it proactively.
- `accessibilityLabel` defaults to `title + description` joined, unless overridden.
- The CTA (when present) is a separate `accessibilityRole="button"` with its own `accessibilityLabel` (the `ctaLabel` text).

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal

- `EtText` — title (`label-primary-semibold`), description (`body-secondary-regular`), CTA (`label-tertiary-semibold`)
- `EtIconV2` — leading icon, fixed size 20
- `useEtoroTheme` — severity color tokens + `primary600` for the CTA

### Related Context

- `EtBanner (components/feedback/banner/)` — promo/marketing compound banner; reach for it when there's no severity/urgency concept.
- `EtToast (components/feedback/toast/)` — transient, auto-dismissing feedback; use `EtAlertBanner` instead when the condition is persistent (stays until the underlying state changes).
